    <exercises>
        <title>4.1: Atoms and subatomic particles</title>

        <exercisegroup>
            <exercise>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        An atom contains 15 protons, 16 neutrons, and 15
                        electrons.
                        What are the charges and locations of the three types of
                        subatomic particles?
                    </p>
                </statement>

                <answer>
                    <p>
                        Protons are +1 and in the nucleus; neutrons are neutral
                        and in the nucleus; electrons are -1 and in the electron
                        cloud.
                    </p>
                </answer>
            </exercise>

            <exercise>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Answer the following and briefly justify your reasoning:
                        An atom contains 15 protons, 16 neutrons, and 15
                        electrons.
                        What are the charges and locations of the three types of
                        subatomic particles?
                    </p>
                </statement>

                <answer>
                    <p>
                        Protons are +1 and in the nucleus; neutrons are neutral
                        and in the nucleus; electrons are -1 and in the electron
                        cloud.
                        A correct justification should connect the answer to the
                        relevant definition, relationship, or calculation from
                        this section.
                    </p>
                </answer>
            </exercise>

